est":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,21095,400,1867,6484,3,702,4126,400,46,3,323,400,1867,14,1808,45157,12947,362,1459,374,26618,11882,504,279,14791,315,22756,400,1867,6484,12947,3555,374,279,18927,429,432,374,12128,311,400,46,3,1091,311,894,315,279,3040,17228,30,220,508,6405,921,2141,7,17,15,15,317,7633,54934,17,20,15,11,16,15,15,29621,7,17,20,15,11,16,15,15,29621,7,17,20,15,4999,16,15,15,29621,4080,17,20,15,4999,16,15,15,29621,21621,317,16119,1188,15,11,15,1106,1502,20912,46,3,44970,15,11,15,701,45,317,1502,20912,32,73315,4080,17,20,15,11,16,15,15,701,69214,1215,2383,20912,33,3,44970,17,20,15,11,16,15,15,701,3944,1215,2383,20912,34,3,44970,17,20,15,4999,16,15,15,701,925,1215,2383,20912,35,73315,4080,17,20,15,4999,16,15,15,701,16844,1215,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nRectangle $ABCD$ has center $O$ and $AB/AD=k$. A point is randomly chosen from the interior of rectangle $ABCD$. What is the probability that it is closer to $O$ than to any of the four vertices?  [asy]\nsize(200);\ndraw((-250,100)--(250,100)--(250,-100)--(-250,-100)--cycle);\ndot((0,0));\nlabel(\"$O$\",(0,0),N);\nlabel(\"$A$\",(-250,100),NW); label(\"$B$\",(250,100),NE); label(\"$C$\",(250,-100),SE); label(\"$D$\",(-250,-100),SW);[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"9d471b9d0d4db906a7bb3d095e3b8ed9d1b764676f46c6a91f7206ad7107f69d"},"seconds":55.312479734420776,"seed":127989663185139574,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to find the probability that a randomly chosen point inside rectangle \\(ABCD\\) is closer to the center \\(O\\) than to any of the vertices \\(A\\), \\(B\\), \\(C\\), or \\(D\\).\n\n1. **Identify the Center and Vertices:**\n   - Let \\(ABCD\\) be a rectangle with \\(AB = a\\) and \\(AD = b\\).\n   - The center \\(O\\) of the rectangle is at \\(\\left(\\frac{a}{2}, \\frac{b}{2}\\right)\\).\n   - The vertices are \\(A(0, b)\\), \\(B(a, b)\\), \\(C(a, 0)\\), and \\(D(0, 0)\\).\n\n2. **Distance to Center \\(O\\):**\n   - A point \\((x, y)\\) inside the rectangle is closer to \\(O\\) if the distance from \\((x, y)\\) to \\(O\\) is less than the distance from \\((x, y)\\) to any vertex.\n   - The distance from \\((x, y)\\) to \\(O\\) is \\(\\sqrt{(x - \\frac{a}{2})^2 + (y - \\frac{b}{2})^2}\\).\n\n3. **Distance to Vertices:**\n   - The distance from \\((x, y)\\) to \\(A(0, b)\\) is \\(\\sqrt{x^2 + (y - b)^2}\\).\n   - The distance from \\((x, y)\\) to \\(B(a, b)\\) is \\(\\sqrt{(x - a)^2 + (y - b)^2}\\).\n   - The distance from \\((x, y)\\) to \\(C(a, 0)\\) is \\(\\sqrt{(x - a)^2 + y^2}\\).\n   - The distance from \\((x, y)\\) to \\(D(0, 0)\\) is \\(\\sqrt{x^2 + y^2}\\).\n\n4. **Conditions for Being Closer to \\(O\\):**\n   - A point \\((x, y)\\) is closer to \\(O\\) if:\n     \\[\n     \\sqrt{(x - \\frac{a}{2})^2 + (y - \\frac{b}{2})^2} < \\sqrt{x^2 + (y - b)^2}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\sqrt{(x - \\frac{a}{2})^2 + (y - \\frac{b}{2})^2} < \\sqrt{(x - a)^2 + (y - b)^2}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\sqrt{(x - \\frac{a}{2})^2 + (y - \\frac{b}{2})^2} < \\sqrt{(x - a)^2 + y^2}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\sqrt{(x - \\frac{a}{2})^2 + (y - \\frac{b}{2})^2} < \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2}\n     \\]\n\n5. **Geometric Interpretation:**\n   - The regions where a point is closer to \\(O\\) than to any vertex form a smaller rectangle centered at \\(O\\) with half the dimensions of \\(ABCD\\).\n   - This smaller rectangle has side lengths \\(\\frac{a}{2}\\) and \\(\\frac{b}{2}\\).\n\n6. **Area Calculation:**\n   - The area of the smaller rectangle is \\(\\frac{a}{2} \\times \\frac{b}{2} = \\frac{ab}{4}\\).\n   - The area of the original rectangle \\(ABCD\\) is \\(ab\\).\n\n7. **Probability Calculation:**\n   - The probability that a randomly chosen point is closer to \\(O\\) than to any vertex is the ratio of the area of the smaller rectangle to the area of the original rectangle:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{\\frac{ab}{4}}{ab} = \\frac{1}{4}\n     \\]\n\nThus, the probability is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
